{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic","id":1404149,"title":"Would you like it if the other WOD games incorporated the \u201cTouchstone\u201d mechanic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-22T18:38:08-07:00","id":1404149,"title":"Would you like it if the other WOD games incorporated the \u201cTouchstone\u201d mechanic?","content":"I think Wraith already has something like it with your fetters.<br /> .<br /> Changling could have Both Mortal and Fae touchstones like The forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T05:09:27-07:00","id":1404223,"title":"","content":"Kinda depends what that means.<br /> <br /> Are we talking everyone gets the V5 version? If so count me out.<br /> <br /> Are we talking the CofD general concept that's basically different (and not even actually present) in every game-line to help them focus on their themes? Sure, if you can make it work without the CofD's common use of Humanity-like mechanics in the rest of the games. Touchstones need mechanics to hook into that are coherent for the story and fun for the game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T05:52:19-07:00","id":1404229,"title":"","content":"It would be counter to the themes of mage and changeling, while it wouldn't be very interesting for werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:45:27-07:00","id":1404284,"title":"","content":"I can see them being neat and useful ways to help add bonuses to characters trying to retain a sense of stability, how to mechanically work them is the question though, to me at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T14:23:45-07:00","id":1404302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1404229#post1404229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be counter to the themes of mage and changeling, while it wouldn't be very interesting for werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends a lot on what you're doing with them.<br /> <br /> If we're using the general idea from CofD, Touchstones are simply things that keep your character rooted in a particular mindset (generally one they want to be in) and the cost of having to maintain that connection in some fashion or negative consequences for losing them. They don't have to be specifically about protecting your sense of humanity.<br /> <br /> Thematically, they can work for most WoD games (even if the struggle on the mechanical side is still very present) because most WoD PCs feel the draw of two or more worlds that they have to balance. Touchstones would help give them an anchor point in those worlds to keep hold of when one is demanding more of their attention than others.<br /> <br /> Ascension has always treated mages as being at risk of detachment from &quot;normal&quot; life because of their fantastic powers and the urge to seclude themselves away where they can use their power without worrying about Sleeper eyes and Consensus. This is one of the oldest forms of hubris in mage society, because in a subjective reality, ignoring the normal world means ceding power in that world to govern how reality works; it's how the Order of Reason/Technocracy became so power... the other mages were ignoring the common folk. The Traditions and Crafts of the modern nights are much greater advocates of having bonds to Sleepers or Sleeper organizations to keep mages focused on important issues.<br /> <br /> Changelings, likewise, feel the constant draw between their mortal lives and the Dreaming. Having specific story elements that emotionally resonate with them in each is highly thematic for them.<br /> <br /> Deviant's Touchstone setup could be very interesting for Apocalypse (rather than using Forsaken's): Deviants have Touchstones based on specific stuff they're actively trying to destroy, and specific stuff they're actively trying to protect. This can highlight the duality of the Garou as violent murder-blenders and Gaia's protectors on a more personal scale. It wouldn't just be, &quot;Combat the Wyrm,&quot; but, &quot;what enemies are you willing to risk Renown, Rank, pack unity, and your long term safety to finish off once and for all?&quot; and what does it say if one of them isn't explicitly a Wyrm creature?<br /> <br /> There's lots of conceptual good stuff there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T14:34:34-07:00","id":1404304,"title":"","content":"I feel there's a lot of fun to be had with the 'reality is my enemy' of mage and changeling that kinda puts you in the deep end. I love the deep end. But I also liked the 'morality is chosen, not ordained' of vampire that wasn't present with v5. Deep end vampires are also very fun... <br /> <br /> Tying yourself down, mechanically, is useful for novice rollplayers. But i think it's a crutch for players who know what they are doing. Break those chains!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T14:57:45-07:00","id":1404308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1404304#post1404304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel there's a lot of fun to be had with the 'reality is my enemy' of mage and changeling that kinda puts you in the deep end. I love the deep end. But I also liked the 'morality is chosen, not ordained' of vampire that wasn't present with v5. Deep end vampires are also very fun...</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if we're talking about CofD over V5, Touchstones don't stop you from being in the deep end, or having morality being chosen rather than ordained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tying yourself down, mechanically, is useful for novice rollplayers. But i think it's a crutch for players who know what they are doing. Break those chains! </div> </div> </div>Touchstones are, ideally, something that creates interesting choices by being a mechanic with a mix of positive and negative consequences.<br /> <br /> Also the &quot;just a crutch,&quot; thing is pretty tired. If mechanics that enforce themes and create mechanical tensions were just a crutch, all of us long time RPers would be using 1 page systems or going freeform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T15:06:55-07:00","id":1404310,"title":"","content":"Honestly no. I have had a bad enough experience with V5 so no thanks please do not fuck it more then needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:24:53-07:00","id":1406783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1404310#post1404310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly no. I have had a bad enough experience with V5 so no thanks please do not fuck it more then needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why didn\u2019t you like V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:02:27-07:00","id":1406799,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> If you do not want to read through the whole thread where the topic whas discussed in all detail <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1389466-v5-my-thoughts-on-touchstones\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...on-touchstones</a><br /> TLDR: They are forced on you and made that you want to kill them ASAP because it would hurt less then keep them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T13:51:25-07:00","id":1406832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1406783#post1406783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why didn\u2019t you like V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>He probably read the book or played it without adequate house rules or something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T14:04:11-07:00","id":1406833,"title":"","content":"I think Touchstones are a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T05:55:55-07:00","id":1407127,"title":"","content":"The only place &quot;Touchstones&quot; (AKA Fetters for this line) made sense in was in Wraith where it was interesting and versatile. Fetters (what VTR and VTM ripped to assort as &quot;Touchstones&quot;) were much, much more better in its home origin. Fetters could be a place, certain area, object, or person/animal and they were graded up to 5- higher being how &quot;attached&quot; your character was to the Fetter. Without Fetters you couldn't stay in the Shadowlands (ghostly reflection of the world that overlaps the living one) for long and be sent back to the Low Umbra.<br /> <br /> Fetters were interesting and strategic because you didn't want your rivals or just plain enemies knowing of them, a Fetter that gets destroyed (maybe using Embody or Outrage, or just possessing a person or animal to then go destroy it) sends you into an Harrowing. Some Wraiths however have a better advantage than others, some could only have Fetters that are merely specific areas and are harder to eliminate (say the Fetter could be only a specific road that you used to drag race at or the general location of where you used to sell drugs at). The worse is when someone very experienced in Lifeweb begins to extort you after they've discovered your Fetter or if due to just the mundanity of chaotic life something just goes wrong with your Fetter in general (say your girlfriend from when you were still alive gets in a bad car accident or the mall that was your Fetter had a huge fire); those situations can bring up very interesting plot hooks in a particular session at any moment.<br /> <br /> This all works when we understand Wraith is a game about being a.. well.. Wraith. Its a game that explores the interesting intrigue, horror, and tales of being a ghost being stuck with unresolvedness. Now Touchstones/Fetters in other games? No, just no.<br /> <br /> The fact that this concept was so hamfisted into VTM in the first place makes absolutely no sense since its a game where you play as immortal entities that increasing become less and less human throughout the ages. Your telling me that a <i>Vampire</i> that will outlive it's Touchstone (that always will be some random human) over and over again MUST always have a Touchstone? Shouldn't they already adapted to a point where they don't have such bothersome inflictions anymore? Touchstones are only something I'd see Toreador having since they are obsessed with human relations and humanity in general, but now every Vampire must have this damned mechanic? Recluse Tzimisce, nomadic Gangrel, or sewer dwelling subterfuge based Noseferatu? Even the thought of putting them in other games sounds like a disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 08-09-2020, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T06:23:47-07:00","id":1407131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1406833#post1406833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Touchstones are a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would be as great as incorporating Humanity as a stat to track on non Vampire Games.<br /> For those that do not get it, in HH2 it whas said you should keep track of your humanity just to see how good of a human you are but unless you get ghouled or the embrace it has no effect despite giving metaknowledge what a cold blooded bastard your character is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T07:41:28-07:00","id":1407139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407131#post1407131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they would be as great as incorporating Humanity as a stat to track on non Vampire Games.<br /> For those that do not get it, in HH2 it whas said you should keep track of your humanity just to see how good of a human you are but unless you get ghouled or the embrace it has no effect despite giving metaknowledge what a cold blooded bastard your character is.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I think Touchstones would defo work for Werewolf or Changeling or even Mage (Wraith already has Fetters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T08:00:21-07:00","id":1407140,"title":"","content":"General, simple, but very important question:<br /> <br /> What problem would the touchstone-like mechanic solve in those gamelines?<br /> <br /> If there is no good and reasonable answer to that, it'd just be bloat added to a game that don't need it, thematically nor mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-09-2020, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T09:21:01-07:00","id":1407148,"title":"","content":"It would give your character greater depth and roleplaying opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:14:10-07:00","id":1407180,"title":"","content":"I know. In Requiem anything that reminds you of your Humanity could be a touchstone.<br /> <br /> \u201c Your character\u2019s Touchstone is a person, place, or thing that reminds her of her humanity, and helps keep her grounded. You\u2019ll need to name a Touchstone, \u201d<br /> <br /> Like one of the examples is the house you used to grow up in.<br /> <br /> I heard some people on the requiem thread discussing a Cigarette Brand as a touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T14:25:31-07:00","id":1407184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407180#post1407180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. In Requiem anything that reminds you of your Humanity could be a touchstone.<br /> <br /> \u201c Your character\u2019s Touchstone is a person, place, or thing that reminds her of her humanity, and helps keep her grounded. You\u2019ll need to name a Touchstone, \u201d<br /> <br /> Like one of the examples is the house you used to grow up in.<br /> <br /> I heard some people on the requiem thread discussing a Cigarette Brand as a touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly with how depend on some brands I am with my form of Child PTSD I would totally allow and believe it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T15:09:08-07:00","id":1407192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407140#post1407140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What problem would the touchstone-like mechanic solve in those gamelines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: Fixing a lack of narrative structure about how vampires connect with Humanity in order to maintain it as part of being human is social and thus the struggle to maintain Humanity in the face of the Beast needs to drag vampires back to humanity in an interactive fashion. The answer to maintaining high Humanity shouldn't be &quot;go be a hermit,&quot; as that removes such efforts from play instead of making different approaches to Humanity having different play experiences.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: Fixing a lack of incentives for behavior beyond Renown farming. Too many of the downsides of Rage are easily avoided by isolationism (yes, this is going to be a running theme), so the game would be better with a game element that reward players for putting their characters in sub-optimal situations that are genre appropriate.<br /> <br /> Mage &amp; Changeling: Fixing a lack of structure around the balancing of living a double life. While lots of people enjoy running around the Umbra as mages, or the Dreaming as changelings, and getting to do wild fantasy adventures instead of dealing with the bleak and depressing normal world, the games are at their strongest when the characters can't just run away like that. Things like that Avatar Storm were done to push back against this, but it was all stick and no carrot; there is a need for something to keep these character grounded to the real world in order to properly execute their themes.<br /> <br /> Wraith (&amp; Orpheus now that it's better integrated in Wraith): As noted, basically has them already.<br /> <br /> Hunter (Imbued): A lot of the places where Touchstones could address certain problems in the game are places where the game needs a serious overhaul anyway. In general though, similar to Mage and Changeling, the Imbued could use a grounding mechanic. There is no mechanical tool for pushing back against the way the mechanics of the game push the PCs to become more and more divorced from normal human life. The metagame too strongly draws a line between being 6/10 dedicated to the Hunt, and being 7+/10 dedicated to it instead of giving room for the lines to be blurrier.<br /> <br /> Demon: Probably doesn't need it beyond existing things, though like Hunter the game needs a new edition badly and that may change it one way or the other fairly easily<br /> <br /> KotE: Largely the same as normal Vampire in this regard. Depending on how any future implementation would go, the temptation to tie them closer to Wraith than Vampire would make this rather natural.<br /> <br /> Mummy: Another basically already as them; though could use some sprucing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:18:51-07:00","id":1407202,"title":"","content":"&quot;Lack of structure&quot; AKA a crutch for when a storyteller can't come up with good ideas for a chronicle by themselves. Touchstones beyond Wraith literally have no point or meaning beyond being a forced mechanical nuisance. Easily what a Touchstone can be is easily just emulated through regular roleplay. Also again, Touchstones don't take into account the various intricates of every splat and their subplats (Clans for Kindred, Tribes for Werewolf, Tradition/Convention for Mage, etc). Do you really believe a nomadic Gangrel always on the prowl will ever need a Touchstone at all or a Euthanatos always trying to gain more insights on Entrophy will bother with one either? Even with that, Touchstones are a really big hamfist for a forced particular line of roleplay you may or may not want. Touchstones for Hunter, Werewolf, and Mage alone sounds like an atrocious idea because their game themes have entirely different focuses.<br /> <br /> The only place where &quot;Touchstones&quot; are remotely good and intriguing is found only in Wraith (where this concept in general all started). Beyond that it should've have stayed in VTR alone, but somehow Touchstones have made its way into VTM and its garbage.<br /> <br /> PS: What you deem &quot;lack of X&quot; isn't a bug, its a feature. Part of tabletops is thinking of interesting scenarios on your own. Touchstones of all aren't even a good baseline for creativity, its just a hamfist turned into hard-written mechanic instead of what could've been roleplayed naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 08-09-2020, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T17:43:38-07:00","id":1407205,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a> technically all the other games had a Prototouchstone in Revised via the Boon True Love where you for having protecting her from your enemies get automatically one success on all Willpower rolls. Though the difference is, that here it whas really a carrot and something that whas properly build in because the TL need to get worked out and it whas not cheap and safe enough so that a Powergamer could just take so you whas able as a ST to have Plotgenerator via an NPC that is the most important thing for a character and a player caring for an NPC or even a PC couple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T03:58:43-07:00","id":1407259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407202#post1407202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Lack of structure&quot; AKA a crutch for when a storyteller can't come up with good ideas for a chronicle by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>All mechanics, rules, settings, themes, and so on are &quot;crutches.&quot; Either you're advocating for pure freeform RP, or you're just tossing around a word to try to make your point sound better than, &quot;I don't like it, so it's inherently bad game design.&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole point of everything in RPGs is because it makes enjoying them easier to having a common reference point instead of forcing everything on the players and GM to come up with themselves.<br /> <br /> Touchstones are also something that, by default, players define, not STs. They're tools for STs to make their chronicles better by having more well defined hooks that the players are deciding are important. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Touchstones beyond Wraith literally have no point or meaning beyond being a forced mechanical nuisance. </div> </div> </div>Every mechanic besides temporary Willpower has no point or meaning beyond being a forced mechanical nuisance. Characters should just be a set of descriptors that all narrative permissions, and Willpower as a dwindling resource when characters want to risk pushing themselves for short term gain at the risk of long term success.<br /> <br /> See? It's easy to blast any and all mechanics with this, because it's a meaningless attempt to paint preference as fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Easily what a Touchstone can be is easily just emulated through regular roleplay. </div> </div> </div>OK, so do you think the WoD games should dump social Backgrounds like Allies, Contacts, Influence, and Mentor? Aren't those all things that can just as easily be emulated through regular role-play?<br /> <br /> If not, why are those important to have a traits, but Touchstones not?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also again, Touchstones don't take into account the various intricates of every splat and their subplats (Clans for Kindred, Tribes for Werewolf, Tradition/Convention for Mage, etc). </div> </div> </div>First, there has never been one implementation of Touchstones. Each implementation so far (whether either of us thinks one is good or bad) has been different.<br /> <br /> Second, why should Touchstones be directly sensitive to such things? Touchstones help refine individual characters and how they relate to the world. Things like subsplats are just going to encourage specific Touchstones over others (depending on the group and which implementation of Touchstones you use).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you really believe a nomadic Gangrel always on the prowl will ever need a Touchstone at all or a Euthanatos always trying to gain more insights on Entrophy will bother with one either? </div> </div> </div>You never need Touchstones, they just help. Even in V5's version which I think was executed extremely poorly.<br /> <br /> I'd expect a nomadic loner Gangrel that lacks any connection to their former life or some new found way anchor their newfound existence would struggle greatly in maintaining control over their Beasts. The fact that this mechanically disincentivizes loner nomads is a good thing to me, because Vampire is designed as a social game and you want to incentivize players to come up with characters that are invested in getting tangled up in the webs of vampire politics. And of course, such Gangrel aren't known, in universe, for being particularly good at maintaining Humanity.<br /> <br /> The Euthanatoic philosophy directly demands that Euthanatos mages maintain bonds to Sleepers in order to avoid becoming obsessed with death and lose sight of the reason they fight to protect the Wheel. One that doesn't already have the equivalent of Touchstones isn't going to get to keep studying Entropy, because their peers and masters are going to pull them aside for some remedial Chodona lessons; and be ready to kill a Euthanatos mage that's shown a disposition for failing to live up to the demands of their creed.<br /> <br /> So... these examples aren't compelling to me as how Touchstones get in the way of anything, esp. as one is actually a case for Touchstones that a Tradition makes in-universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even with that, Touchstones are a really big hamfist for a forced particular line of roleplay you may or may not want. Touchstones for Hunter, Werewolf, and Mage alone sounds like an atrocious idea because their game themes have entirely different focuses. </div> </div> </div>Did you even read post #5 on this thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you deem &quot;lack of X&quot; isn't a bug, its a feature. </div> </div> </div>No they're not. You can argue that you don't personally feel the need for mechanics in them, but I was responding to a post asking what Touchstones would solve for specific game lines.<br /> <br /> It's not a feature that the only way for VtM vampires to maintain high Humanity is to go not be fun to play, it's a bug that denies interesting gaming of high Humanity vampires struggling to stay so in the light of vampire politics and human reality.<br /> <br /> It's not a feature that the strongest incentive-based influence on character behavior - the Renown system - doesn't actually result in the thematic core that the game says it's about.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> I get that you disagree, but if you're not going to put any work into it, what's the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of tabletops is thinking of interesting scenarios on your own. Touchstones of all aren't even a good baseline for creativity, its just a hamfist turned into hard-written mechanic instead of what could've been roleplayed naturally. </div> </div> </div>Again, you can make such empty bland declarations about any mechanic.<br /> <br /> RPGs promote creativity within limitations (this is an extremely common approach beyond RPGs, as many people find it easier to be creative with limits over absolute freedom). Touchstones (and again, the general concept, not a specific implementation of them) are just another way to provide the limits of frameworks and structures that help most people be creative because such elements narrow things down and make it easier to decide on things to do. That's why a lot of people buy these big books with lots of rules in them.<br /> <br /> A long standing debate in RPG design are social mechanics (including even having social Attributes/Abilities/Skills/etc.). Some people want to feel free to act out their characters, and others feel that player social aptitude shouldn't override how the character is written; esp. for people that aren't necessarily great at social skills but want to get to play someone that is. I'm very firmly in the second camp. And in general I say have rules and not need them, than need rules and not have them.<br /> <br /> The point to all this being, from any reasonable perspective, being creative within the limitations of the rules as set forth by the game is role-playing naturally, and demanding less structure on your role play is actually the radical position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:05:13-07:00","id":1407309,"title":"","content":"So, DnD 5e has this background system that encourages rollplaying quite nicely. You've got your bond to the party, your ideal, your flaw; it's not a perfect system, but it's not supposed to be: you can completely ignore it, or make up your own additions. It's just there to help newbies ground their characterizations. <br /> <br /> Vampire could copy this quite well. Do I trust the current lot to do that? Not exactly. They seem to have some funny ideas about a few things. But it's a lot better than suggesting a character needs specific attachments. Vampire personalities should seem real, not something wholly unique to the vampire state","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T09:48:05-07:00","id":1407316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so do you think the WoD games should dump social Backgrounds like Allies, Contacts, Influence, and Mentor? Aren't those all things that can just as easily be emulated through regular role-play?<br /> <br /> If not, why are those important to have a traits, but Touchstones not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because those backgrounds aren't forced at all and aren't explicitly necessary. Beyond that those backgrounds are actually tactically useful in terms of general mechanic and storytelling. Touchstones as it is in VTM 5e is just going Twilight. Instead of botching out Humanity they could've revamped it to not degrade over every little thing instead having your entire humanity centered around an annoying Touchstone-Human. The kicker to all this? Having a Touchstone is mandatory unlike &quot;Allies, Contacts, Influence, and Mentor.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones help refine individual characters and how they relate to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't, all it does is give ever player some Bella they now have to fawn over less their humanity tanks. In all the World of Darkness lines there are much better ways of how PCs interact/relate to the world from just general story driven tasks or miscellaneous encounters alone. Those however can be decided whether it can be explore into at a greater length or toned down for other important aspects of a chronicle. Now with Touchstones they are always lingering forced nuisance that has to be attended to or else your character goes bust.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that this mechanically disincentivizes loner nomads is a good thing to me, because Vampire is designed as a social game and you want to incentivize players to come up with characters that are invested in getting tangled up in the webs of vampire politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this is one of the glaring problems with Touchstones- it can force someone who wants to take a different route to one that now is mechanically fatwa'd into the game at large with no choice. Being a &quot;loner Gangrel&quot; obviously doesn't mean they don't get embroiled in Vampire politics (since obviously in every VTM session unless your doing it solo with only one ST and one person playing) since the basic fiat is that your in a coterie doing objectives. Beyond that though this theoretical loner Gangrel when the coterie's business is all said and done goes back to their domain in solitude to not deal with kine or other Kindred. Also Touchstones by itself are always humans, what does it have to do with Vampire politics to begin with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Euthanatoic philosophy directly demands that Euthanatos mages maintain bonds to Sleepers in order to avoid becoming obsessed with death and lose sight of the reason they fight to protect the Wheel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even with that its still only meant to be general interactions with Sleepers and not to a point where it conflicts with their studies. Of course avoiding Jhorr has to be on the checklist too, but I see no real use of Touchstones for an Euthanatos. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a feature that the only way for VtM vampires to maintain high Humanity is to go not be fun to play, it's a bug that denies interesting gaming of high Humanity vampires struggling to stay so in the light of vampire politics and human reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly does this mean? Pre-V5 before regular humanity was scrapped- being high humanity is a choice in a society based on a general urban underworld that is Vampire at large. How do you know for certain that the people who play as high humanity Vampires deliberately don't have fun or even to assume it CAN'T be fun? And what you say alone is already a facet in pre-V5 Vampire where people DO struggle to still have high humanity while trying to do tasks they don't push them to the brink for some who play that way. Why do you say it doesn't exist at all? Wut? It doesn't matter anyway since V5 just rekt'd out Humanity altogether for Touchstones so you bringing this up doesn't make sense. <br /> <br /> Generally Touchstones could be tolerable if it was just another miscellaneous background or trait you could choose. Now its a locked in mandatory char-trait that MUST be had since it got ripped and bootstrapped from VTR to VTM without fleshing it out entirely. None of the other oWoD titles (besides Wraith where this idea originated and is the best at) deserve this Touchstone fate as VTM has suffered through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T12:08:03-07:00","id":1407346,"title":"","content":"Somehow this discussion remind of discussion about why Classic WoW is so much (not) better then Retail or Vice versa. My salt is, what I ment with the touchstone mechanic should get the same treatment as humanity whas that humanity is effectiv useless in non Vampire Games so yeah from my opinion the other lines can get it, if it would mean, you just get contacts that are only bringing you boons because there is no beast inside you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:02:40-07:00","id":1407367,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25523_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25523\" data-vbnamecard=\"25523\">Shakanaka</a><br /> <br /> OK, before I do a whole big rebuttal thing...<br /> <br /> You do get that I despise how V5 implemented Touchstones right? That I'm talking about the general concept of adding Touchstones to the WoD, not replicating that specific method?<br /> <br /> Because right now, it just feels like you're letting your dissatisfaction with how V5 did things override any reasonable discussion to be had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:56:07-07:00","id":1407382,"title":"","content":"It's not about just V5, I just feel that Touchstones is a mechanic that isn't really needed at all for any of the lines. Its something they should've stayed unique to CofD and should've been ported over. oWoD and CofD are different lines for various reasons. How &quot;it was done&quot; in V5 is just a misunderstanding of function because the developers of the edition just gobbled up stuff from CofD without phasing if it would actually work for oWoD. Even worse by how you picture it they apparently did it worse than how it was in CofD. Generally though I don't agree with Touchstones as this sort of port feature from CofD that now has to be mainstay mechanic for oWoD at all.<br /> <br /> If it does stay for continuous editions for Vampire and for possible new stuff for other lines, it should merely be somesort of Background and not something that has to be mechanic that MUST be done for a character/sheet to complete. You bring up &quot;Allies, Contacts, Influence, and Mentor&quot; previous but fail to remember that there completely optional and not necessary. The &quot;general concept&quot; of Touchstones or more aptly described &quot;Fetters&quot; found in Wraith: The Oblivion is the only place in oWoD where such a concept is viable or even interesting. Touchstones are a disaster for VTM because its explicitly forcing a type of playstyle or specific roleplay no matter what as now this mechanic only originally meant for CofD is now tied to Humanity with no other alternative. For other gamelines? There is literally no point in the addition of Touchstones for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T16:12:18-07:00","id":1407393,"title":"","content":"I agree with Shakanaka. After thinking about it again Touchpoints in other gameslines would be only like those minor allies from Mage and in comparison to humanity which would make at least sense to track if it would not be an uproar to &quot;reward&quot; Characters with the embrace. So mayby for this reasons they want to implement them though I stay with my saying, just give players one or two points of Allies only for Minor allies for free and the thing would be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T18:09:29-07:00","id":1407408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407382#post1407382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about just V5, I just feel that Touchstones is a mechanic that isn't really needed at all for any of the lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how am I supposed to square that so much of your response is focused on the V5 implementation of Touchstones? They're not even valid critiques of VtR Touchstones (which is, you know, a Background you can choose to invest in even if you get a free Touchstone at start), let alone all the other Touchstone variants in the CofD that could be used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> oWoD and CofD are different lines for various reasons. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But they also overlap enough that this isn't a sufficient argument. There's plenty of things in the CofD that could be used to make the WoD a stronger game... people have been porting rules over since 2004 because they decided the new rules had something to offer but didn't feel like converting over fully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generally though I don't agree with Touchstones as this sort of port feature from CofD that now has to be mainstay mechanic for oWoD at all. </div> </div> </div>Do you have a strong reason for this beyond personal taste though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You bring up &quot;Allies, Contacts, Influence, and Mentor&quot; previous but fail to remember that there completely optional and not necessary. </div> </div> </div>You still have Background points you need to assign to finish your character. Generation (a long contentious Background) is the only one that couldn't be shunted off to &quot;role-playing&quot; and doesn't come with a set of interpersonal connections your character has to explain how those Backgrounds manifest for your character. You can't not take Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;general concept&quot; of Touchstones or more aptly described &quot;Fetters&quot; found in Wraith: The Oblivion is the only place in oWoD where such a concept is viable or even interesting. Touchstones are a disaster for VTM because its explicitly forcing a type of playstyle or specific roleplay no matter what as now this mechanic only originally meant for CofD is now tied to Humanity with no other alternative. For other gamelines? There is literally no point in the addition of Touchstones for them. </div> </div> </div>I've pointed out multiple times places where the concept of Touchstones (which is actually separate from Fetters at this point) are viable and interesting. You haven't really engaged in any of those ideas directly.<br /> <br /> There are definitely points for the addition of Touchstones; even if you don't value them personally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407393#post1407393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After thinking about it again Touchpoints in other gameslines would be only like those minor allies from Mage and in comparison to humanity which would make at least sense to track if it would not be an uproar to &quot;reward&quot; Characters with the embrace. So mayby for this reasons they want to implement them though I stay with my saying, just give players one or two points of Allies only for Minor allies for free and the thing would be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, what about things like Deviant's Touchstones that I said would be a good idea for WtA?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T08:50:45-07:00","id":1407521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1404149-would-you-like-it-if-the-other-wod-games-incorporated-the-\u201ctouchstone\u201d-mechanic?p=1407408#post1407408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what about things like Deviant's Touchstones that I said would be a good idea for WtA?</div> </div> </div> </div>May be or good thing or not, my burned child experience say it would not be but I do not know if I failed the language or the WtA Hobbyknowledge test but I can not imagine anything about it or put a finger on it how it would work ingame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T12:47:51-07:00","id":1408221,"title":"","content":"Continuing the idea that Touchstones are an extension of Fetters. Fetters were used to anchor your wraith to the mortal world, to give them reason, drive, a purpose to not spiral down into oblivion. As you resolve your fetters you are then able to theoretically transcend.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Vampire Touchstones help ground a vampire, keep them from being lost to the Beast. I personally believe that they should be like Requiem touchstones and be places or entities, not just a specific person. A vampire can have a touchstone of his mortal family, one of which he focuses his attention on. if something happens to that specific member, they die of old age or are killed, the vampire goes through a grieving process and then latches onto a new member to follow.<br /> <br /> I think Werewolf could have touchstones that are broken into categories, you could have one that connects/reminds you of your humanity, one that connects/reminds you of your bestial/animal nature and one that connects/binds you to your spiritual nature. If you loose your spiritual touchstone, you risk Harano. if you loose your bestial touchstone, you find it more difficult to shape shift. If you loose your humanity touch stone, you frenzy much more easily.<br /> <br /> For Mage, you could turn their tools of magic into touchstones. They represent their paradigm, their connection to reality. if you loose touchstones, you are more susceptible to madness or Paradox.<br /> <br /> Fore Changeling, you can have Touchstones connecting them to both their Fae self and the Human self, if the Fae touchstones are destroyed, they can more easily gain banality, if they loose their human touchstones, they risk more Beldam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}